<section class="block-section do">
  <span class="section-tag">Do</span>
  <h2>Today's work: everyone does this</h2>
  <div class="callout factstorm">
    <div class="callout-title">Factstorm: four minutes</div>
    <p>Factstorm, then compare. Three rounds:</p>
    <p><strong>Round 1</strong> (4 min, groups): everything you know about the Cooum river. Facts, memories, things your family says about it; all of it goes on the list.</p>
    <p><strong>Round 2</strong> (3 min, whole class): we ask the class AI platform the same question and capture its list beside ours.</p>
    <p><strong>Round 3</strong> (5 min): three comparisons. What did the AI have that the room didn't? Pick ONE and verify it before trusting it. What did the ROOM have that the AI didn't? Notice what kind of knowledge that is. And the quiet question: given what the room produced in four minutes, what was the AI actually FOR here? Keep all three answers; today's source work is about exactly this river.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="callout task">
    <div class="callout-title">The task: Two sources, one river</div>
    <p>Read these two sources about the Cooum. Run OPVL on each. Then write one sentence that names the Limitation that matters most for each source, and one sentence saying which source you would cite for what.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Government:</strong> Chennai Rivers Restoration Trust, <a href="https://crrt.tn.gov.in/cooum_restoration" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cooum restoration page</a></li>
      <li><strong>News:</strong> DT Next, <a href="https://www.dtnext.in/news/chennai/trouble-runneth-deep-in-dying-adyar-cooum-rivers-797027" target="_blank" rel="noopener">"Trouble runneth deep in dying Adyar, Cooum rivers"</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
